exclusions:
  panel-datasource-rule:
    reason: >-
      Datasource UIDs are pinned on purpose (azure-monitor-oob for Application
      Insights, admin-prod-obs-amw for the blackbox probes). A ${datasource}
      variable saves the value "default"; the default datasource in
      dis-grafana-prod is Azure Monitor rather than Prometheus, so Grafana
      silently falls back to the first Prometheus datasource -- a dis-core AMW
      that holds no probe data -- and the availability panels render empty with
      no error. The dashboard also mixes two datasources in one view, which a
      single template variable cannot express.
    entries:
      - dashboard: "Infoportal — Service Health (Prod)"
  template-datasource-rule:
    reason: >-
      No datasource template variable by design; see panel-datasource-rule.
    entries:
      - dashboard: "Infoportal — Service Health (Prod)"
